"""Combo bổ sung — chủ đề Survey (AI soạn mới, 2026-10).

Mỗi combo: topic, cat, src (nguồn đối chiếu chủ đề), items = [(mã dạng câu, câu hỏi, bài mẫu IH)].
Mã dạng câu giống class_meta.py: D R P PR PF M X CC C2 RA RV RP RE I N.
Câu hỏi viết lại theo cách hỏi quen thuộc của OPIc; không chép từ nguồn nào.
Bài mẫu: nhân vật giống bộ câu hỏi của lớp (≈30 tuổi, kiểm tra chất lượng ở nhà máy điện tử,
sống ở Thái Nguyên với vợ và con gái 5 tuổi).
"""

C = [
    dict(id="concerts-1", topic="concerts", cat="survey", src="SRC-0301", items=[
        ("D", "You indicated in the survey that you enjoy going to concerts or performances. Tell me about a place where you like to see live performances. Where is it? What does it look like? Describe it in as much detail as possible.",
         """Well, the place I like most is an outdoor stage in the city square, right in the center of Thai Nguyen. It's not a fancy concert hall, but I think that's why I like it. The stage is quite big, with huge speakers on both sides and colorful lights hanging above it. In front of the stage, there's a wide open area where people can stand, and on the sides, there are rows of plastic chairs for older people and families with kids. Around the square, there are lots of food stalls selling grilled corn, sausages and milk tea. When there's a show, the whole area is full of people and the atmosphere is really lively. It feels more like a festival than a formal concert."""),
        ("R", "What do you usually do when you go to a concert? Tell me what you do before, during, and after the show.",
         """Usually, I check the program online a few days before, and if the singer is someone my wife likes, we ask my parents-in-law to take care of our daughter. On the day of the show, we try to arrive about an hour early, because parking gets really crowded. Before it starts, we grab something to eat from the food stalls and find a good spot, not too close to the speakers. During the show, I mostly just sing along and take a few videos, but I try not to stay on my phone the whole time. After it ends, we wait a bit for the crowd to leave, and then we usually stop at a small cafe on the way home to talk about our favorite songs."""),
        ("M", "Tell me about the most memorable concert or performance you have ever been to. When was it, who did you go with, and what made it so special? Give me all the details.",
         """The most memorable one was a free concert in Hanoi about eight years ago, to celebrate National Day. I went with three of my close friends from university, and we took the bus from Thai Nguyen in the afternoon. When we got there, the area around the lake was already packed, so we had to stand really far from the stage. At first I was a little disappointed, because we could barely see the singers. But then something unexpected happened. It started raining heavily, and instead of leaving, everyone just stayed and kept singing together in the rain. The singer on stage even came down closer to the crowd. We were completely soaked, but honestly, it was one of the happiest nights of my life. Whenever I hear those songs now, I still remember that night and my friends laughing in the rain."""),
    ]),
    dict(id="hiking-1", topic="hiking", cat="survey", src="SRC-0301", items=[
        ("D", "In the survey, you indicated that you go hiking or trekking. Tell me about a place where you like to go hiking. Where is it, and what is the trail like?",
         """My favorite place for hiking is Tam Dao, a mountain area about an hour and a half from where I live. The main trail starts near a small town on the mountain and goes up through a thick forest. The path isn't too long, maybe three or four kilometers, but some parts are quite steep and there are a lot of stone steps. Along the way, you can hear birds and small streams, and the air is much cooler than in the city. At the top, there's a TV tower and a flat area where you can sit and look down at the valley. On a clear day, the view is amazing, with green hills and clouds below you. It's a perfect place to escape the heat and noise of the city."""),
        ("PF", "Tell me how you first got interested in hiking. When did you start, who did you go with, and how has your interest changed since then?",
         """I actually started hiking quite late, about four years ago. Before that, I thought hiking was only for young backpackers. But one of my coworkers kept talking about a trip his team made to Ba Vi mountain, and he showed me photos of the view from the top. So the next time they went, I joined them. To be honest, the first trip was really hard. I wasn't fit at all, and I had to stop every few minutes to catch my breath. But when we reached the top, I felt so proud of myself. After that, I started walking more during the week to get in better shape. Now I go hiking every two or three months, and these days I sometimes take my wife and daughter on easier trails. So it has changed from a challenge into a family hobby."""),
        ("X", "Have you ever had a problem while you were hiking? Maybe you got lost, the weather changed, or someone got hurt. Tell me what happened and how you dealt with it.",
         """Yes, I have. About two years ago, I went hiking in Tam Dao with two friends. We started late, around two in the afternoon, which was a big mistake. On the way down, it suddenly got foggy and started to rain, and it became dark much earlier than we expected. Then one of my friends slipped on a wet rock and twisted his ankle. He could still walk, but very slowly. At first we panicked a little, because we had almost no phone signal. Luckily, I had a small flashlight in my bag, so I walked in front to light the path, and the other friend helped him walk. We moved really slowly and finally got back to the town after about two hours. Since then, I always start early, check the weather, and bring a flashlight and a first aid kit."""),
    ]),
    dict(id="hiking-2", topic="hiking", cat="survey", src="SRC-0301", items=[
        ("R", "What do you usually bring with you when you go hiking? How do you prepare for a hiking trip?",
         """I usually prepare the night before. First, I check the weather forecast, because rain can make the trail really slippery. Then I pack a small backpack with two bottles of water, some bananas and bread, and a light raincoat. I also bring a power bank, a flashlight and a few bandages, just in case. For clothes, I wear comfortable sports clothes and my hiking shoes, which have a good grip. In the morning, I eat a proper breakfast, and we try to leave home around six so we can start walking before it gets too hot. That's pretty much my routine."""),
        ("PR", "Tell me about the last time you went hiking. Where did you go, who did you go with, and what happened during the hike?",
         """The last time I went hiking was about a month ago, on a small hill by Nui Coc Lake, not far from Thai Nguyen city. I went with my wife and our daughter, because the trail there is short and quite easy. We left home early in the morning and got there at around seven. The first part of the trail was flat and shady, so my daughter ran ahead and kept picking up leaves and small stones. Later, it got steeper, and she asked me to carry her on my back for a while, so my legs were really tired. When we reached the top, we could see the whole lake below us, and we sat there and had a little picnic with sticky rice and fruit. On the way down, we stopped to take a lot of pictures. It was simple, but it was a really lovely family morning."""),
        ("M", "Tell me about a memorable hiking experience you had. Where did you go, who were you with, and what made that hike so unforgettable?",
         """The most unforgettable hike was when I climbed Fansipan, the highest mountain in Vietnam, about three years ago. Most tourists take the cable car, but my friends and I decided to walk the trail. It took us two days. On the first day, we walked for almost eight hours through forests and bamboo, and we stayed overnight in a simple camp on the mountain. It was freezing, and I could hardly sleep. On the second day, we woke up at four and continued climbing in the dark. When we finally reached the top, the sun was rising above a sea of clouds. Everyone just stood there in silence for a minute. I was exhausted, but I felt like I had achieved something really big. I still keep a photo of that sunrise as my phone's wallpaper."""),
    ]),
    dict(id="music-ext-1", topic="music", cat="survey", src="SRC-0301", items=[
        ("D", "You indicated that you enjoy listening to music. Where and how do you usually listen to music? What kind of device do you use? Describe it for me.",
         """I mostly listen to music on my phone, using a music streaming app. I have a pair of wireless earbuds that I bought last year, and I use them almost every day, especially during my lunch break or when I go for a walk in the evening. They're small and white, and the sound is surprisingly good for the price. At home, we also have a Bluetooth speaker in the living room. It's round and about the size of a coconut. On weekends, I connect it to my phone and play music while I'm cleaning or cooking. My daughter loves it, because she can dance around the living room to her favorite children's songs."""),
        ("CC", "How has the way people listen to music changed over the years? How did people listen to music in the past, and how is it different now?",
         """It has changed a lot. When I was a kid, my family had an old cassette player, and my father kept a box of tapes of old Vietnamese songs. If you wanted a new album, you had to go to a music shop and buy a tape or a CD. Later, when I was in high school, everyone downloaded MP3 files from the internet and copied them onto small MP3 players. These days, almost nobody buys CDs or downloads music files anymore. People just use streaming apps on their phones, and they can listen to millions of songs anytime, anywhere. Another big difference is how we discover music. In the past, we heard new songs on the radio or TV, but now most people find new music through short videos on social media. A song can become famous overnight just because of a dance challenge. I think it's more convenient now, but songs also seem to be forgotten much faster."""),
        ("M", "Tell me about a special experience you had related to music. Maybe you heard a song that meant a lot to you, or something memorable happened while you were listening to music.",
         """One special memory is from my wedding about seven years ago. My wife and I didn't hire a professional singer. Instead, a group of my close friends from university secretly practiced a song for weeks. They chose an old love song that my wife and I often listened to when we were dating. During the party, the MC suddenly announced a surprise, and my friends walked onto the stage with a guitar. One of them could barely sing, so everyone laughed, but they kept going until the end. My wife started crying, and to be honest, I almost cried too. Even now, whenever that song comes on, we look at each other and smile. For me, it's not just a song anymore. It's a memory of our friends and the beginning of our family."""),
    ]),
    dict(id="parks-ext-1", topic="parks", cat="survey", src="SRC-0301", items=[
        ("D", "Tell me about a park near your home. What does it look like, and what kinds of facilities does it have?",
         """There's a park about five minutes from my apartment, and it's called the Youth Park. It's built around a small lake, and there's a walking path of about one kilometer that goes all the way around the water. Along the path, there are lots of big trees and benches where people can rest. On one side of the lake, there's a playground with slides and swings, and next to it, there's an outdoor gym with simple exercise machines. Near the entrance, there's a big open square where people do aerobics or play badminton in the evening. The park isn't very large, but it's clean and well looked after, so it's a really nice place to relax after work."""),
        ("R", "What do people usually do in parks in your country? Describe what you see people doing in the park at different times of the day.",
         """It really depends on the time of day. Early in the morning, around five or six, the park is full of older people. They walk around the lake, do tai chi, or practice simple exercises together. Some young people go jogging before work. During the day, it's pretty quiet, because most people are at work or school, so you mostly see a few people resting on the benches. Then in the late afternoon, it gets busy again. Parents bring their kids to the playground, students hang out with friends, and some people play badminton or football. In the evening, there are groups of women doing aerobics to loud music. So, except for the middle of the day, parks in Vietnam are usually busy and lively."""),
        ("X", "Have you ever had any problems or unexpected situations at a park? Tell me what happened and how you handled it.",
         """Yes, one time I had a pretty scary experience. Last summer, I took my daughter to the park near our apartment in the evening. She was playing on the slide with other kids, and I was sitting on a bench nearby, checking a message on my phone. When I looked up, I couldn't see her anywhere. My heart started racing. I ran around the playground calling her name, but she wasn't there. Then I asked a security guard for help, and he made an announcement through the park's speaker. A few minutes later, a woman brought my daughter back. She had followed a puppy all the way to the other side of the lake. I was so relieved that I hugged her really tightly. Since that day, I never look at my phone when she's playing, and I taught her to stay where I can see her."""),
    ]),
    dict(id="beach-ext-1", topic="beach", cat="survey", src="SRC-0301", items=[
        ("D", "You said in the survey that you like going to the beach. Tell me about a beach you like to visit. Where is it, and what makes it special?",
         """The beach I like the most is Sam Son beach in Thanh Hoa province. It takes about four hours by car from my home, so we usually go there once a year in the summer. The beach is very long and wide, with soft yellow sand and quite gentle waves, so it's safe for kids. Along the beach, there's a long road full of hotels, seafood restaurants and small shops selling swimsuits and souvenirs. What makes it special to me is the atmosphere in the evening. When the sun goes down, the whole beach becomes really lively. Families sit on the sand, kids build sandcastles, and there are street food vendors everywhere. It's not the most beautiful beach in Vietnam, but it's affordable and fun."""),
        ("PR", "Tell me about the last time you went to the beach. When was it, who did you go with, and what did you do there?",
         """The last time I went to the beach was in June this year. My company organized a summer trip for all employees, so I went with my wife, my daughter, and many of my coworkers' families. We took a big tour bus to Do Son beach in Hai Phong. On the first afternoon, we went swimming, and my daughter spent hours building sandcastles with other kids. In the evening, the company held a party on the beach with a barbecue and team games. My team won the tug of war, which was really fun. The next morning, I woke up early and walked along the beach to watch the sunrise. Then we had a big seafood lunch before going home. It was short, but it was a great chance to relax and get to know my coworkers' families better."""),
        ("X", "Tell me about a problem you had while you were at the beach. What happened, and how did you solve it?",
         """I remember a problem we had on a beach trip about two years ago. We went to Cua Lo beach for a long weekend, and on the second day, I took my wife and daughter swimming. After about an hour, we went back to where we had left our things on the sand, and my wife's bag was gone. It had her phone, some cash and our hotel key card inside. At first, we were really worried. I asked the people sitting near us, but nobody had seen anything. Then I went to the lifeguard station and the beach security office to report it. Luckily, about an hour later, they called us. One of the beach cleaners had found the bag near a trash bin. The cash was gone, but the phone and the key card were still there. After that, we always leave one person to watch our things, or we keep valuables in the hotel safe."""),
    ]),
    dict(id="domestic-ext-1", topic="domestic_trips", cat="survey", src="SRC-0301", items=[
        ("R", "When you travel within your country, how do you usually prepare for the trip? Tell me about the things you do before you leave.",
         """Since I travel with my wife and daughter, we usually plan about a month in advance. First, we decide where to go and check the weather for that time. Then I book the hotel online, usually a place with a pool, because my daughter loves swimming. If it's far, like Da Nang, I book plane tickets early to get a cheaper price. A week before the trip, my wife makes a list of things to pack, and the night before, we pack everything together. I also check the car, or I book a taxi to the airport. And finally, I download offline maps on my phone, just in case we lose signal."""),
        ("PR", "Tell me about the most recent trip you took within your country. Where did you go, and what did you do each day?",
         """The most recent trip was to Ha Long Bay last April, during the national holiday. We drove there on the first morning, and it took about three hours. In the afternoon, we checked into our hotel and went for a walk along the beach. On the second day, we joined a boat tour around the bay. We saw lots of limestone islands, visited a huge cave with colorful lights inside, and even tried kayaking for about thirty minutes. My daughter was a bit scared at first, but then she loved it. For lunch, we had fresh seafood on the boat. On the last morning, we took the cable car up to the top of a hill and saw the whole bay from above. Then we drove back home in the afternoon. It was tiring because of the holiday crowds, but it was totally worth it."""),
        ("X", "Have you ever had an unexpected problem during a trip in your country? Tell me what happened and how you dealt with it.",
         """Yes. Last year, we drove to Sa Pa for a weekend trip, and halfway up the mountain road, our car got a flat tire. It was raining, the road was narrow and there was no repair shop nearby. My wife was worried because it was getting dark. I had never changed a tire by myself before, so I called a roadside service, but they said it would take at least two hours. Then a local man on a motorbike stopped and offered to help. He showed me how to use the jack and change to the spare tire, and it took us about twenty minutes. I tried to give him some money, but he refused and just told us to drive carefully. We arrived at the hotel late, but safe. After that trip, I watched a few videos and practiced changing a tire, so I'm ready next time."""),
    ]),
    dict(id="overseas-ext-1", topic="overseas_trips", cat="survey", src="SRC-0301", items=[
        ("R", "What do you usually do to prepare for a trip abroad? Tell me about everything you do before you leave your country.",
         """Traveling abroad needs a lot more preparation. First, I make sure our passports are still valid and check if we need a visa. Then I compare flight prices on a few websites and book the tickets about two months in advance. After that, I book hotels close to the city center or near public transportation. A week before we leave, I exchange some money into the local currency and buy a travel SIM card online. I also make a simple plan for each day, with a list of places to visit and restaurants to try. And the night before, I check everything again, like passports, tickets and chargers, because forgetting something abroad can be a big headache."""),
        ("PR", "Tell me about the last time you traveled to another country. Where did you go, who did you go with, and what did you do there?",
         """The last time I went abroad was two years ago, when my wife and I went to Bangkok in Thailand for five days. It was our first trip without our daughter, because she stayed with her grandparents. On the first day, we visited the Grand Palace and a few famous temples. It was extremely hot, but the buildings were beautiful, with gold roofs and colorful decorations. The next day, we went shopping at a huge weekend market and tried lots of street food, like mango sticky rice and grilled pork. One evening, we took a boat along the river and had dinner while watching the city lights. On the last day, we bought some gifts for our family and coworkers. It was a short trip, but it felt like a second honeymoon."""),
        ("X", "Have you ever had a problem while traveling abroad? Tell me about what happened and what you did to solve it.",
         """Yes, on that trip to Bangkok, we had a problem at the airport on the way home. When we arrived at the check-in counter, the staff told us that our flight had been canceled because of a technical issue, and there was no other flight until the next afternoon. I was really stressed, because I had to go back to work the next day. First, I called my manager to explain the situation and asked for one more day off. Luckily, he was very understanding. Then I asked the airline staff what they could offer us. They gave us a free hotel room near the airport and meal vouchers. We actually ended up having a nice dinner and a good rest. The next day, we flew home without any problems. I learned that staying calm and asking politely really helps."""),
    ]),
    dict(id="vacation-home-ext-1", topic="vacation_home", cat="survey", src="SRC-0301", items=[
        ("R", "You indicated that you spend your vacations at home. What do you usually do when you have a vacation at home? Tell me about a typical day.",
         """When I have a vacation at home, I try to make it different from normal days. On a typical day, I sleep in until about eight, which is a luxury for me. Then we go out for a big breakfast, usually pho, or my wife and I make fried eggs and bread at home. In the morning, I often do small jobs around the apartment, like fixing something or cleaning the balcony. In the afternoon, we take our daughter to the park or to a nearby shopping mall. And in the evening, we cook something special, then watch a movie together on the sofa. It's simple, but it helps me recharge."""),
        ("PF", "When did you first start spending your vacations at home instead of traveling? Why did you start doing that, and how do you feel about it now?",
         """I started spending vacations at home about five years ago, when our daughter was born. Before that, my wife and I traveled almost every holiday. But with a newborn baby, traveling was just too difficult and too tiring. So we decided to stay home during the long holidays. At first, I felt a little bored and kind of jealous when I saw my friends' travel photos online. But after a while, I started to enjoy it. We didn't have to deal with traffic jams, crowded beaches or expensive hotels. Now, even though our daughter is older, we still spend most short holidays at home and only travel once or twice a year. Honestly, I think resting at home is sometimes better than traveling, because we come back to work feeling really refreshed."""),
        ("M", "Tell me about a memorable vacation you spent at home. What did you do, and why do you remember it so well?",
         """The most memorable one was last summer. We had a week off, but it rained heavily almost every day, so we had to stay home the whole time, and at first, it felt really boring. But then my wife and I decided to make it fun. We turned our living room into a different place every few days. One day, it was a camping site. We built a tent with blankets and chairs, turned off the lights and told stories with a flashlight. Another day, it was a restaurant, and my daughter took our orders with a little notebook. We also learned to bake bread together, and the first loaf was so hard that we laughed for minutes. It wasn't the holiday we had planned, but it brought us really close as a family. When we look at the photos now, we always smile."""),
    ]),
    dict(id="housing-ext-1", topic="housing", cat="survey", src="SRC-0301", items=[
        ("D", "Tell me about the neighborhood where you live. What is it like? What kinds of places and people are there?",
         """I live in a fairly new residential area on the edge of Thai Nguyen city. My apartment building is one of about ten buildings in the same complex, and most of the people here are young families like mine. On the ground floor, there are a few small shops, a pharmacy and a convenience store, which is really convenient. Across the street, there's a primary school, so in the morning, it's full of parents dropping off their kids. Behind the complex, there's a small park with a playground. The neighbors are friendly, and we often chat in the elevator or at the playground. It's not very fancy, but it's safe and comfortable."""),
        ("R", "What kinds of household chores do you do at home? Who does what in your family, and how often do you do them?",
         """In my family, we share the chores. My wife usually cooks dinner, because she's much better at it than me. In return, I wash the dishes every evening and take out the trash. On weekends, we clean the whole apartment together. I usually vacuum and mop the floors, and my wife cleans the bathroom and the kitchen. We do the laundry about three times a week with the washing machine, and I'm in charge of hanging the clothes on the balcony. Even our daughter has a small job. She puts her toys away and helps set the table. I think sharing the chores makes things fairer, and we get them done faster."""),
        ("CC", "How is the home you live in now different from the home you lived in when you were a child? Tell me about the differences in detail.",
         """They're totally different. When I was a child, I lived in a small house in the countryside with my parents, my grandparents and my younger brother. The house had only two rooms, and we all slept on wooden beds in the same room. The kitchen was a separate small building outside, and my grandmother cooked with firewood. We had a big yard with chickens and a garden of vegetables. Now I live in an apartment on the seventh floor with my wife and daughter. It's much smaller than my old yard, but it's more modern and comfortable. We have air conditioning, a gas stove, and our own bedrooms. On the other hand, I miss the fresh air and the space. In the past, I could run around outside all day, but my daughter mostly plays inside. So I think my childhood home had more freedom, while my home now has more convenience."""),
    ]),
    dict(id="movies-ext-1", topic="movies", cat="survey", src="SRC-0301", items=[
        ("D", "You indicated that you like going to the movies. Tell me about the movie theater you usually go to. Where is it, and what does it look like inside?",
         """The movie theater I usually go to is on the top floor of a shopping mall near my house. It's a modern cinema with six screening rooms. When you walk in, there's a big lobby with posters of new movies and a counter where you can buy popcorn and drinks. There are also some ticket machines, so you don't have to wait in line. The screening rooms are pretty comfortable. The seats are soft and red, and there are couple seats in the back row. The screens are big and the sound is very loud and clear. It's a great place to escape the heat on summer weekends."""),
        ("R", "What do you usually do before and after you watch a movie at the theater? Tell me about your routine from beginning to end.",
         """Usually, I go to the movies with my wife on Saturday evenings. A few days before, we pick a movie and book seats on the cinema's app, because the good seats sell out fast. On the day, we have dinner at a restaurant in the same mall, often hotpot or Korean barbecue. About fifteen minutes before the show, we buy a big popcorn and two drinks and find our seats. After the movie, we usually walk around the mall for a while and talk about the story, especially the ending. Sometimes we disagree, which makes it more fun. Then we ride home and check on our daughter."""),
        ("X", "Have you ever had a problem at a movie theater? Maybe something went wrong with your tickets, your seats, or the movie itself. Tell me what happened.",
         """Yes, one time we had a funny problem. My wife and I booked tickets online for a new action movie on a Saturday night. When we arrived at our seats, there was already another couple sitting there, and they also had tickets for the same seats. At first, both couples were a little annoyed, and we showed each other our tickets. Then I looked more carefully and realized that my tickets were actually for the next day. I had chosen the wrong date when booking. I felt really embarrassed and apologized to them. I went to the counter and explained the problem. The staff were very kind. They said they couldn't refund the tickets, but they changed them to two other seats for the same show for a small fee. Now I always check the date twice before I pay."""),
    ]),
    dict(id="walking-ext-1", topic="walking", cat="survey", src="SRC-0301", items=[
        ("D", "You indicated that you enjoy walking. Where do you usually go walking? Describe the place and tell me why you like walking there.",
         """I usually walk along the river near my apartment, the Cau River. There's a wide concrete path next to the water that goes on for about three kilometers, with trees and street lights on one side. In the evening, the breeze from the river makes it much cooler than other parts of the city. You can see people fishing, kids riding bicycles and couples sitting on the benches. I like walking there because it's peaceful and the view is relaxing, especially at sunset when the sky turns orange over the water. It's the best way to clear my mind after a long day at the factory."""),
        ("R", "How often do you go walking? Who do you usually walk with, and what do you do while you're walking?",
         """I try to go walking about four or five times a week, usually after dinner, around eight o'clock. On weekdays, I often walk by myself, because my wife is helping our daughter get ready for bed. When I'm alone, I put on my earbuds and listen to podcasts or English lessons, which is a good way to practice my English, actually. I usually walk for about forty minutes. On weekends, the whole family goes together, and my daughter rides her small bicycle while we walk next to her. We stop at a small shop to buy ice cream on the way back."""),
        ("M", "Tell me about a memorable experience you had while you were walking. What happened, and why do you remember it?",
         """I remember one evening last year when I was walking along the river by myself. It was pretty late, and there weren't many people around. Suddenly, I saw an old man sitting on a bench who looked confused. When I asked if he was okay, he said he couldn't remember the way home. I felt worried, so I stayed with him and asked for his name. He had a small card in his wallet with his son's phone number, so I called it right away. His son was really worried, because his father had been missing for two hours. About fifteen minutes later, he arrived on his motorbike and thanked me again and again. On my way home, I kept thinking about my own parents. That night, I called them, even though it was late, just to hear their voices."""),
    ]),
]
